
<% content_for :title, "Press Send. | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="press-send-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="press-send-hero">
    <div class="press-send-hero-inner">

      <p class="press-send-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / ADDICTION / PERSPECTIVES / PRESS SEND
      </p>

      <div class="press-send-hero-grid">

        <div class="press-send-hero-copy">
          <p class="press-send-kicker">THE STORIES / 03</p>

          <h1>
            <span>PRESS</span>
            <span class="press-send-title-accent">SEND<span class="press-send-period">.</span></span>
          </h1>

          <p class="press-send-tagline">
            DRUNK TEXTS.<br>
            IMPULSIVE WORDS.<br>
            SOBER CONSEQUENCES.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="press-send-phone" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="press-send-phone-top">
            <span class="press-send-phone-dot"></span>
            <span>MESSAGES</span>
            <span>•••</span>
          </div>

          <div class="press-send-bubble incoming">
            You good?
          </div>

          <div class="press-send-bubble outgoing">
            Yeah I'm fine
          </div>

          <div class="press-send-bubble outgoing">
            actually...
          </div>

          <div class="press-send-bubble outgoing last">
            <span class="press-send-typing">
              <i></i><i></i><i></i>
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="press-send-phone-bottom">
            <span>MESSAGE</span>
            <span class="press-send-send-arrow">↑</span>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <div class="press-send-hero-footer">
        <span>AN ADDICTION JOURNAL</span>
        <span>SCROLL TO READ ↓</span>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- INTRO -->
  <section class="press-send-section press-send-intro-section">
    <div class="press-send-container">

      <p class="press-send-section-number">
        01 / BEFORE YOU HIT SEND
      </p>

      <h2>
        ONE TEXT.<br>
        <span>TOO MANY WORDS.</span>
      </h2>

      <div class="press-send-prose">
        <p>
          There are things you say when you're drunk that you
          wouldn't say sober. Sometimes you mean them. Sometimes
          you don't. Sometimes you wake up and wonder what the
          fuck you were thinking.
        </p>

        <p>
          A message takes seconds to send. The consequences can
          last considerably longer.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- JOURNAL -->
  <section class="press-send-section press-send-journal-section">
    <div class="press-send-container">

      <p class="press-send-section-number">02 / THE STORY</p>

      <h2>
        THE THINGS<br>
        <span>I CAN'T UNSEND.</span>
      </h2>

      <div class="press-send-journal">

        <p class="press-send-journal-label">
          PERSONAL JOURNAL
        </p>

        <p>
          The time is 3AM. Like faulty electricity, I’m
          browning or blacking out. My feelings are running
          away from me—I’m either angry or crying. I’m sending
          my friends Stephen King novels, saying things I
          don’t mean. I’m emotional. I’m being mean; I’m acting
          like my life is the biggest tragedy and that I have
          been completely abandoned by everyone that I love.
          I am acting like nobody loves me or cares about me.
        </p>

        <p class="press-send-impact">
          I’m being ridiculous.<br>
          And I believe everything I’m typing.
        </p>

        <p>
          I’m being ridiculous. And I believe everything I’m
          typing. I’m typing and typing. I keep going, word
          vomiting and making errors in spelling, with word
          choices, and grammar. I think I’m being slick, but
          to the sober observer, it’s plainly obvious that
          I’m intoxicated.
        </p>

        <p>
          I’m crossing boundaries and breaking rules.
        </p>

        <div class="press-send-messages">
          <p>“Don’t text me at this hour.”</p>
          <p>“Don’t say this to me.”</p>
          <p>“What are you doing?”</p>
          <p>“Why would you say that to me?”</p>
          <p>“Did you really mean to say that?”</p>
        </div>

        <p>
          “Don’t text me at this hour.” “Don’t say this to me.”
          “What are you doing?” “Why would you say that to me?”
          “Did you really mean to say that?” So many things
          stirred up just because I was drunk and decided
          to have false feelings, my brain playing tricks
          on me in the moment of drunkenness. Causing a ruckus,
          making others upset by what I sent them.
          If this were an Olympic sport, I’d have more
          medals than Michael Phelps.
        </p>

        <div class="press-send-olympics">
          IF THIS WERE AN OLYMPIC SPORT,<br>
          I'D HAVE MORE MEDALS<br>
          THAN MICHAEL PHELPS.
        </div>

        <p>
          I texted friends after I felt wronged by things
          they did that were in their best interest.
        </p>

        <div class="press-send-question">
          “WHY DID YOU DO THIS TO ME?”
        </div>

        <p>
          “Why did you do this to me?” I asked. Then I
          proceeded to attempt to go for the jugular,
          trying to hurt them as much as they hurt me,
          once again saying things I didn’t mean in a
          pathetic attempt to cause them pain that
          matched mine in that drunk moment.
          It didn’t work. It backfired, and communication
          was cut for awhile. So, the heartbreak only
          increased. Drunk ideas are never good ideas.
        </p>

        <p class="press-send-impact">
          Drunk ideas are never good ideas.
        </p>

        <p>
          And the shame and regret. After waking up from
          a blackout, the dread of looking at my cell phone
          and wondering who did I text and what did I send
          them. Who did I call? Picking up the phone, I half
          cover the screen as I open my inbox. I occasionally
          breathed a sigh of relief, but normally that was
          not the case.
        </p>

        <div class="press-send-dread">
          <span>THE MORNING AFTER</span>
          <p>
            WHO DID I TEXT?<br>
            WHAT DID I SEND?<br>
            WHO DID I CALL?
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>
          It turned out to be generally harmless, but sometimes
          there would be messages that I regretted. I needed
          to do damage control; I needed to answer for those
          messages. I needed to begin to do repairs for what
          I said or for the time I dialed someone up.
        </p>

        <p class="press-send-final-story">
          I couldn’t even list all of the times that this
          happened, so I wrote a general story to encompass
          them all.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- CLOSING REFLECTION -->
  <section class="press-send-section press-send-reflection-section">
    <div class="press-send-container">

      <p class="press-send-section-number">
        03 / THE AFTERMATH
      </p>

      <h2>
        YOU CAN DELETE<br>
        <span>THE MESSAGE.</span><br>
        NOT THE IMPACT.
      </h2>

      <div class="press-send-prose">

        <p>
          The messages were sent. The arguments happened.
          The boundaries were crossed. And the people
          receiving those messages had to deal with
          the consequences of my intoxicated behavior.
        </p>

        <p>
          I may not have meant everything I said,
          but the words were still mine to answer for.
          Apologizing was only part of the repair.
          Whether someone chose to forgive me or
          continue the relationship was ultimately
          their decision.
        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <section class="press-send-end">
    <div class="press-send-container">

      <p class="press-send-end-title">
        PRESS SEND<span>.</span>
      </p>

      <p>
        THE MESSAGE WAS SENT.
        THE STORY IS STILL BEING WRITTEN.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO ADDICTION PERSPECTIVES",
          addiction_perspectives_path,
          class: "press-send-back" %>

    </div>
  </section>

</main>
